WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:07.560
It is often believed that in relationships,
opposites attract.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:13.309
Like two magnets compelled together by the
force of their opposite poles, two humans

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:20.990
are attracted into a bond of love and intimacy
when they are opposites of one another.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:26.520
The point of a relationship is to have someone
to share life with.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:33.079
Not only that, but someone to help navigate
through and improve life with.

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:39.010
Perhaps it is possible that opposites are
often believed to attract because they create

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.770
a dynamic exchange of personal improvement.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:50.370
If a couple is to some level opposite of one
another, when each person brings their views

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:58.460
and personality to the table, they can provide
alternative insight and perspective into each

00:00:58.460 --> 00:00:59.519
other’s lives.

00:00:59.519 --> 00:01:06.950
A check-and-balance of sorts where the contrast
between each partner provides equilibrium

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:10.400
to each others’ personality type.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:17.910
This is of great value because our personalities
can be very elusive and consuming.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:23.450
After we have become attached and conditioned
by our personality at an early age, they tend

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.110
to run away with us.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:32.540
We should appreciate and embrace our unique
personalities, but their force can often cause

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:36.620
us to become complacent and stagnant.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:43.120
They can close us off from considering and
executing improvements in our self and our

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.120
life.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:50.870
And therefore, it is very beneficial to have
someone who can help us consider and mediate

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:56.020
our personality from a different vantage point.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:02.250
The likely truth is that a happy long-term
relationship forms out of a balance of being

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.490
both opposite and similar.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:11.750
An elaborate mix of complementary and contrasting
personality traits and values, layered onto

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:18.430
one another in an order that provides balance
to both individuals.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:24.420
But regardless of how true it is or isn’t
that opposites attract, there will always

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:31.510
be some level of difference in the personalities
and perspectives of two people.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:37.310
And what’s more important than anything
else is both partners being aware of each

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:44.790
other’s differences and possessing the willingness
to work through them and meet in the middle.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:53.140
For a relationship to survive where both individuals
feel inspired, challenged, and benefited,

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:59.510
each side must be willing to give up a little
bit of themselves in order to receive a little

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.760
bit from their partner.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:08.030
To be open to the ways in which their partner
lives and the potential benefits it can have

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:12.280
on their life and the relationship as a whole.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:19.291
It is this exchange that brings balance to
each person, neutralizes complacency, and

00:03:19.291 --> 00:03:28.100
facilitates a relationship of lasting and
potent love.

